{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tater Up</strong> is a chaotic multiplayer party platformer where up to <strong>4 potatoes</strong> race, climb, and sabotage each other in a gravity-defying vertical world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The goal is simple:<br><strong>Reach the top before your friends do.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Actually doing it? That\u2019s the hard part.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jump, dash, roll, and recover your way upward through floating city debris, moving platforms, fans, cannons, and absurd obstacles - all while <strong>physically interfering with other players</strong> to slow them down or send them falling.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There\u2019s no straight path upward. Along the climb, players encounter <strong>mini-game islands</strong> like <strong>soccer</strong> and <strong>hockey</strong>, where competition temporarily shifts from climbing to chaotic side challenges. These moments break the pace, create rivalries, and often completely flip the outcome of a match.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There\u2019s no tutorial, no hand-holding, and no safety net - just pure <strong>\u201cfuck around and find out\u201d</strong> gameplay where every fall is funny, every recovery is tense, and every victory feels earned.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Up to 4-player multiplayer chaos</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Vertical platforming</strong> instead of traditional racing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skill-based movement</strong>: jump, dash, roll, recover</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Mini-games embedded into the world</strong> (soccer, hockey, and more)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Physics-driven player interaction</strong> \u2014 push, bump, sabotage</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Low-poly, colorful, toon-styled visuals</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fast, replayable matches built for laughs and rivalry</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Tater Up</i> is about momentum, mistakes, and that one perfect push that sends your friend all the way back down.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3989920?t=1769025307","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3989920/1441117d4622eaf26c6a90119fc776d924697466/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1769025307","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3989920/03f1376b157af81c5962c5fc097bfdd69528980c/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1769025307","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3989920/03f1376b157af81c5962c5fc097bfdd69528980c/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1769025307","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Multi-player","id":1},{"description":"PvP","id":49},{"description":"Online PvP","id":36},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tater Up</strong> is a chaotic multiplayer party platformer where up to <strong>4 potatoes</strong> race, climb, and sabotage each other in a gravity-defying vertical world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The goal is simple:<br><strong>Reach the top before your friends do.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Actually doing it? That\u2019s the hard part.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jump, dash, roll, and recover your way upward through floating city debris, moving platforms, fans, cannons, and absurd obstacles - all while <strong>physically interfering with other players</strong> to slow them down or send them falling.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There\u2019s no straight path upward. Along the climb, players encounter <strong>mini-game islands</strong> like <strong>soccer</strong> and <strong>hockey</strong>, where competition temporarily shifts from climbing to chaotic side challenges. These moments break the pace, create rivalries, and often completely flip the outcome of a match.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There\u2019s no tutorial, no hand-holding, and no safety net - just pure <strong>\u201cfuck around and find out\u201d</strong> gameplay where every fall is funny, every recovery is tense, and every victory feels earned.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Up to 4-player multiplayer chaos</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Vertical platforming</strong> instead of traditional racing</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skill-based movement</strong>: jump, dash, roll, recover</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Mini-games embedded into the world</strong> (soccer, hockey, and more)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Physics-driven player interaction</strong> \u2014 push, bump, sabotage</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Low-poly, colorful, toon-styled visuals</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fast, replayable matches built for laughs and rivalry</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Tater Up</i> is about momentum, mistakes, and that one perfect push that sends your friend all the way back down.</p>","developers":["Ash and Pause"],"genres":[{"description":"Casual","id":"4"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3989920/fdca8e219d0bd142bebe5ce31b9ef1efe4e10a65/header.jpg?t=1769025307","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/3989920/1036407677/2612e55d1a4feea3fbd5398fc15e25c11475a80c/1768141669/dash_av1.mpd?t=1768329568","dash_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/3989920/1036407677/2612e55d1a4feea3fbd5398fc15e25c11